Rebuild from extracted source
The original zero-build rebuilt the extracted source in a new output directory,
including its required self-hosted compiler fixed point. All 78 rebuilt
artifacts match the final reference build byte for byte, including both native
platforms, compilers, boot payloads and ISO. The rebuilt zero-web-check passed
35 checks; rebuilt zero-inspect-check passed 13757 header checks.
Rebuilt artifacts:
 /tmp/zero-support/validation-0.16/source-package/restored-build

Scope
This packaging check does not establish physical Windows, VirtualBox or hardware
compatibility. Module documentation records native Linux, Wine and graphical
display validation and its limits. The native browser remains a bounded local
viewer without HTTP/HTTPS fetching. Header inspection does not verify payload
integrity or execute applications. Ideas 723 and 898 came from the readable
1-1000 catalogue; unavailable newer titles were not treated as implemented.

This receipt is outside the archive to avoid self-referential hashing.
Private validation orchestration is not part of the published source.
Git repository and release publication are separate parent operations.
